WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:08.684
"Who's ready to greet the guest of honor?" the bandleader asked the party crowd.

2
00:00:08.685 --> 00:00:11.679
Everyone went wild, cheering.

3
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:19.681
"Here she is at long last, Allyzooba Delta5X of Astralia!"

4
00:00:19.682 --> 00:00:22.364
Ally glided onto the dance floor.

5
00:00:22.365 --> 00:00:26.580
She twirled, showing off her new dress.

6
00:00:26.581 --> 00:00:29.625
"I'm so happy to finally be back home on—"

7
00:00:29.626 --> 00:00:34.961
"That does not compute," Alpha interrupted.

8
00:00:34.962 --> 00:00:38.643
Ally opened her eyes and groaned.

9
00:00:38.644 --> 00:00:41.315
She wasn't back on Astralia.

10
00:00:41.316 --> 00:00:47.523
She was in her bed in her pod, still on Earth.

11
00:00:47.524 --> 00:00:53.999
"It's time for your morning dance party," Alpha said as music blared from her speakers.

12
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.912
"Not today, Alpha." Ally got out of bed.

13
00:01:00.913 --> 00:01:06.225
"My dream made me sad. I thought I'd be home by now."

14
00:01:06.226 --> 00:01:12.494
"Disappointment is a logical response," Alpha said. "Advice: consider the positives."

15
00:01:12.495 --> 00:01:16.937
Ally sighed. "I'll try to stay positive.

16
00:01:16.938 --> 00:01:21.244
I have a good friend in Mateo, who'll keep my identity a secret.

17
00:01:21.245 --> 00:01:25.408
He also offered to help me get parts so I can fix the pod.

18
00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:29.048
Oh, I forgot to tell you—he's stopping by this morning."

19
00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:35.309
"Warning!" Alpha blared. "Astralian camouflage will not work with an alien on board."

20
00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:40.764
"Calm down. He won't be here long—I have to go to work," Ally replied.

21
00:01:40.765 --> 00:01:48.036
"He just wants to see my pod. I'll camouflage it as soon as we leave."

22
00:01:48.037 --> 00:01:50.386
Mateo arrived a short while later.

23
00:01:50.387 --> 00:01:54.706
His eyes went wide as he looked around.

24
00:01:54.707 --> 00:01:59.287
"This pod is awesome. I wish we could go flying!"

25
00:01:59.288 --> 00:02:06.238
"Proposal," Alpha said. "If the human can assist in repairing the pod, a short flight can be authorized."

26
00:02:06.239 --> 00:02:13.265
"Whoa!" Mateo said. "I've got a smartphone, but it's not as smart as your computer!"

27
00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:18.519
"Alpha knows everything there is to know in the entire universe," Ally said.

28
00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:21.546
"You can ask her anything."

29
00:02:21.547 --> 00:02:28.074
"Anything?" Mateo said. "Hmm. Bethany and I have been dating for one month.

30
00:02:28.075 --> 00:02:32.020
Got any super fun ideas for an anniversary surprise?"

31
00:02:32.021 --> 00:02:36.593
"Allyzooba is a superior resource for that question," Alpha replied.

32
00:02:36.594 --> 00:02:41.772
"Astralians must use their Astral minds to help others in the universe."

33
00:02:41.773 --> 00:02:45.361
"I'll come up with a fun idea," Ally said.

34
00:02:45.362 --> 00:02:56.101
"But for now we should focus on the pod parts. Alpha, can you print out the list again?"

35
00:02:56.102 --> 00:02:59.575
When it was ready, Mateo looked it over.

36
00:02:59.576 --> 00:03:05.936
"I'm not sure how to get rocket fuel, but I think we can make beta-booster coils from old mattress springs.

37
00:03:05.937 --> 00:03:08.344
And I know exactly where to get some."

38
00:03:08.345 --> 00:03:12.176
"Great!" Ally said. "Let's get going."

39
00:03:12.177 --> 00:03:16.425
Ally grabbed her meld medallion and hurried to the door.

40
00:03:16.426 --> 00:03:21.463
"Warning," Alpha called. "Do not forget to camouflage the pod."

41
00:03:21.464 --> 00:03:27.387
"I know." Ally rolled her eyes. "Let's go, Mateo."

42
00:03:27.388 --> 00:03:32.842
"Wait!" Mateo said. "You still look like an Astralian."

43
00:03:32.843 --> 00:03:39.928
"Oops!" As Ally led the way out of the pod, she slipped her meld medallion over her neck.

44
00:03:39.929 --> 00:03:45.823
She immediately changed into human form.

45
00:03:45.824 --> 00:03:51.184
"Watching you transform like that is amazing!" Mateo said.

46
00:03:51.185 --> 00:03:55.896
"You mean like this?" Ally said.

47
00:03:55.897 --> 00:04:02.979
Mateo laughed as Ally toggled between her Astralian and human forms until she got dizzy.

48
00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:08.119
"Phew! That's enough of that!"

49
00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.370
Ally and Mateo headed downtown.

50
00:04:10.371 --> 00:04:15.479
Along the way they noticed some new sculptures installed in different spots.

51
00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.210
There was a giant red heart with the words Love Your Mother (Earth);

52
00:04:19.211 --> 00:04:25.211
an oversize sunflower; and three sheep grazing on grass in a traffic median.

53
00:04:25.212 --> 00:04:28.544
"What are these sculptures?" Ally asked.

54
00:04:28.545 --> 00:04:34.352
"Sandville hired an artist to create public art with an ecological theme," Mateo said.

55
00:04:34.353 --> 00:04:39.648
"And the coolest thing is, she's reusing stuff she finds around town."

56
00:04:39.649 --> 00:04:44.010
"Everything gets reused on Astralia," Ally said.

57
00:04:44.011 --> 00:04:48.290
"I'm glad to see humans thinking about wasting less on Earth."

58
00:04:48.291 --> 00:04:52.384
"Speaking of not wasting stuff . . ." Mateo held up his phone.

59
00:04:52.385 --> 00:04:58.699
"The Sandville Mattress Factory offers old springs for free."

60
00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.893
"Springs?" Ally said, confused.

61
00:05:01.894 --> 00:05:05.450
"They're coils," Mateo said.

62
00:05:05.451 --> 00:05:09.721
"Oh! Do we have time to check it out before I go to work?"

63
00:05:09.722 --> 00:05:16.794
"I think so." Mateo spoke to his phone: "Mira, where is Sandville Mattress Factory?"

64
00:05:16.795 --> 00:05:22.417
"1515 West 19th Street," Mateo's phone replied.

65
00:05:22.418 --> 00:05:26.153
"You have an Alpha too!" Ally said.

66
00:05:26.154 --> 00:05:35.609
Mateo laughed. "Yep. But like I said, Mira isn't nearly as smart as Alpha!"

67
00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:43.981
A short while later, Ally and Mateo arrived at the diner with a bag of springs.

68
00:05:43.982 --> 00:05:49.201
Ray was sitting in a booth, surrounded by cookbooks.

69
00:05:49.202 --> 00:05:52.116
"What's all this, Papi?" Mateo asked.

70
00:05:52.117 --> 00:05:55.120
"I've got a problem," Ray said.

71
00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:58.662
"The League of Rocket Scientists wants to hold its annual gala here."

72
00:05:58.663 --> 00:06:01.806
"Why is that a problem?" Mateo asked.

73
00:06:01.807 --> 00:06:08.930
Ray dropped his head into his hands. "Because it's next week!"

